---
/* L00 - what this repo is, and what a decision model is not. One writer: the figures workstream A. */
---

<figure class="fig">
  <div class="fig__frame">
    <img
      class="fig__picture"
      src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}illustrations/L00.jpg`}
      alt="A line drawing of two hands sliding a paper ticket into one of four open trays arranged in a row on a counter, with a stack of tickets waiting beside them."
    />
    <svg
      class="fig__svg"
      viewBox="0 0 640 340"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="L00-fig-title L00-fig-desc"
    >
      <title id="L00-fig-title">One message in, a number on every option, and a threshold the caller draws</title>
      <desc id="L00-fig-desc">
        On the left a small card stands for one customer message, drawn as three short
        rules. An arrow runs right into a square labelled model, with swappable written
        under it. A second arrow runs right again into a distribution over four fixed
        options, drawn as four horizontal bars that start at a common origin on a scale
        labelled probability, with the names billing, technical, sales and other
        written to the left of them. The first bar reaches furthest; the other three stop
        well short of it. A vertical prussian line labelled 0.6 threshold crosses the
        first bar and misses the other three; a note says the bar lengths are
        illustrative. The bars rise into place one after another, the threshold line then
        draws itself down across them, and a prussian dot pulses where the line crosses
        the first bar.
      </desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="L00-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path d="M 0 0 L 10 5 L 0 10 z" fill="var(--color-ink-45)" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- the state: one customer message -->
      <rect x="34" y="104" width="108" height="76" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="46" y1="122" x2="128" y2="122" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="46" y1="138" x2="128" y2="138" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <line x1="46" y1="154" x2="104" y2="154" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="34" y="196" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">one customer message</text>

      <!-- into the model -->
      <path d="M 146 142 L 184 142" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L00-arrow)" />

      <!-- the model: swappable, the same questions every time -->
      <rect x="190" y="98" width="88" height="88" fill="var(--color-ground)" stroke="var(--color-ink)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="234" y="136" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="12" fill="var(--color-ink)">model</text>
      <text x="234" y="154" text-anchor="middle" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">swappable</text>
      <text x="190" y="202" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the same question set</text>

      <!-- out of the model: a distribution over a fixed set of options -->
      <path d="M 282 142 L 320 142" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-ink-45)" stroke-width="1" marker-end="url(#L00-arrow)" />

      <line x1="418" y1="204" x2="618" y2="204" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="418" y="222" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">probability</text>

      <text x="336" y="86" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">billing</text>
      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.2s;" x="418" y="74" width="150" height="14" fill="var(--color-prussian-tint)" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />

      <text x="336" y="116" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">technical</text>
      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.4s;" x="418" y="104" width="56" height="14" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />

      <text x="336" y="146" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">sales</text>
      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.6s;" x="418" y="134" width="36" height="14" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />

      <text x="336" y="176" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="11" fill="var(--color-ink-70)">other</text>
      <rect class="m-rise" style="--m-duration: 0.7s; --m-delay: 0.8s;" x="418" y="164" width="26" height="14" fill="var(--color-ground-deep)" stroke="var(--color-rule)" stroke-width="1" />

      <!-- the caller's threshold, drawn after the answers arrive -->
      <path class="m-draw" style="--m-length: 148; --m-duration: 1s; animation-delay: 1.2s;" d="M 538 54 L 538 198" fill="none" stroke="var(--color-prussian)" stroke-width="1" />
      <text x="544" y="62" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-prussian)">0.6 threshold</text>

      <circle class="m-pulse" style="--m-duration: 1.2s; --m-delay: 2s;" cx="538" cy="81" r="4" fill="var(--color-prussian)" />

      <text x="336" y="248" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">a number on every option, not one answer</text>
      <text x="336" y="264" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">bar lengths are illustrative</text>

      <text x="34" y="330" font-family="var(--font-mono)" font-size="10" fill="var(--color-ink-45)">the model supplies the numbers; the caller decides what to do with them</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="fig__caption">
    <span class="edge-code">figure L00</span>
    <span class="fig__caption-text">One customer message goes in and a number comes back on every fixed option, and the threshold that turns a number into an action belongs to the caller, not to the model.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  /* scoped to this figure */
  .fig__svg {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
